15 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating study participant selection: 323 patients initially at a hemodialysis center, 129 assessed for eligibility, 8 excluded, 121 met criteria, 32 excluded for not providing a fecal sample, and 89 included for final microbiome analysis, split into HDUP group \(45 participants\) and HDNUP group \(44 participants\).) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a rarefaction curve of observed features by number of sequences sampled, with HDNUP \(red\) consistently higher than HDUP \(blue\), shaded bands indicating confidence intervals. Panel B presents a rarefaction curve for Shannon Index, again with HDNUP in red and HDUP in blue, showing HDNUP's higher diversity across sequencing depth, with shaded confidence intervals.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a PCOA plot with samples represented by red circles and blue triangles, divided by dashed ellipses. Panel B displays a similar NMDS plot using the same color scheme and groupings. Panel C presents a notched boxplot comparing three groups labeled Between, HDUP, and HDNUP with similar box distributions and a non-significant p-value. Panel D shows a comparable notched boxplot for the same groups, with more distinct box separation and a significant p-value.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Heatmap visualization comparing two groups, HDUP and HDNUP, in microbiome data. Panel A displays clustering by phylum, while panel B shows clustering by genus. Color gradients from blue to red represent relative abundance values, with corresponding color bars and dendrograms indicating hierarchical relationships. Group labels and taxonomic names are presented along the axes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a stacked bar chart comparing relative abundances of different bacterial phyla between HDUP and HDNUP groups, with Firmicutes predominating. Panel B presents a bar graph showing mean relative abundances and standard deviations for major phyla, highlighting differences and associated p-values between the two groups. A color legend lists each phylum.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a stacked bar chart comparing the relative abundance of bacterial genera in two groups, HDUP and HDNUP, with each genus represented by a different color. Panel B presents a grouped bar chart of specific genera abundances between HDUP \(red\) and HDNUP \(blue\), displaying significant p-values above genera where differences are notable. A genus legend is included for reference on panel A's right side, and a group legend for panel B's right side.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a horizontal bar chart comparing LDA scores \(log 10\) for different bacterial taxa, with HDNUP group in red and HDUP group in green. Panel B displays a circular cladogram highlighting bacterial taxa enriched in each group, with clusters shaded red for HDNUP and green for HDUP. Both panels depict differences in gut microbiota composition between the two groups.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Bar chart comparing relative abundances of functional gene categories between HDNUP and HDUP groups, with categories listed on the left, colored bars for each group, and corresponding adjusted p-values and log2 fold changes displayed on the right.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
